Original commit body from fdc9a2100d317886f9491e3a7142072d542724ae:

`measure-catalogue-reach.py` had only ever run on Python; pointed at any other
language it emitted Python source containing that language's module names,
resolved nothing, and its positive control correctly refused to report. This
adds per-language call-site emitters with per-language FORM vocabularies.

THE FIRST GO RUN REPORTED 0 OF 210 AND THE CONTROL REFUSED TO PUBLISH IT. The
probe's own banner read `// generated by scripts/measure-catalogue-reach.py`,
which matches `supply_chain.is_likely_minified` heuristic 3 —
/(Generated by|@generated|DO NOT EDIT)/i anywhere in the first five lines — and
classifies the file Tier.DERIVED. Controlled, identical body: no header → 2
boundaries, `// leading comment` → 2, `// generated by …` → 0; bisected to the
exact phrase. Filed as INV-pogob, which also records that supply_chain.py holds
TWO generated-file predicates with different patterns that disagree about this
file, and that the same header on a .py file changes nothing.

RESULTS (docs/measurements/0002-catalogue-reach-multilanguage.md):
  go          162/210 (77.1%) — ALL 45 method-kind entries unattributed
  javascript  182/187 (97.3%) with a module-scope require; 4/187 (2.1%) with
              the identical call and a function-local one — a 35x fixture-shape
              effect, and the lazy-require shape is real code
  java        129/142 (90.8%) via the STATIC form, ZERO via the instance form
  python      194 both / 16 dotted / 0 bare / 5 neither — improved from the
              recorded 153/16/41/5 with the denominator unchanged

Neither INV-suril nor INV-gijis is settled by this and both say so in the
record: the Java probe supplies a module hint, so the no-module-hint gate
INV-suril names is never reached; and INV-gijis's implied FP channel produces
no edge at all on the obvious shape.

Forms are per-language because they have to be — Go has one idiomatic form and
Java's pair is instance/static, not dotted/bare. Go additionally gets a go.mod
and one file per import path, because a single file importing all 22 packages
the catalogue names is neither idiomatic nor, as it turned out, measurable.

